{
  "configuration_id": "config_013",
  "reason": "Evidence: The jump from singleprofile (~0.53) to multiprofile+transformer+weighted (0.725, config_025) is dramatic, but we cannot yet attribute this improvement to the image modality versus the multiprofile RNA representation alone. RNA singleprofile alone achieved 0.520, and multimodal singleprofile only reached 0.532, suggesting the image contributes very little in singleprofile mode. Question: config_013 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, transformer) isolates whether the multiprofile+transformer RNA pipeline alone can approach 0.725, or whether the image encoder (imagenet_vit_l) is providing a meaningful complementary signal in the multiprofile setting. Why this is the best next experiment: It changes only one factor (removing the image) from the current best configuration, cleanly separating the contribution of the image modality from the profile/aggregation gains. If rna_only multiprofile+transformer approaches 0.72, the image is unnecessary and we should focus budget on RNA encoder and profile choices; if it falls well short, the multimodal fusion is justified and we should exploit that direction. This single experiment resolves the most fundamental design uncertainty before spending further budget on encoder or fusion variations."
}

